{"name":"Freshly Roasted Coffee","hex":"#663322","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"freshly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Recently, newly.","In a rude or impertinent manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freshly"},{"term":"roasted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by roasting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of roast"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roasted"},{"term":"coffee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beverage made by infusing the beans of the coffee plant in hot water. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A serving of this beverage."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale brown colour, like that of milk coffee.","Of a table: a small, low table suitable for people in lounge seating to put coffee cups on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee","wikidata":"Q8486"},{"title":"Freshly","blocks":[{"text":"Freshly was a New York City-based convenience food delivery company that delivered throughout the contiguous United States. It was acquired by Nestlé in October 2020 and was shut down in January 2023."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freshly","wikidata":"Q104845347"},{"title":"Roasting","blocks":[{"text":"Roasting is a cooking method that uses dry heat where hot air covers the food, cooking it evenly on all sides with temperatures of at least 150 °C (300 °F) from an open flame, oven, or other heat source. Roasting can enhance the flavor through caramelization and Maillard browning on the surface of the food. Roasting uses indirect, diffused heat, and is suitable for slower cooking of meat in a larger, whole piece. Meats and most root and bulb vegetables can be roasted. Any piece of meat, especially red meat, that has been cooked in this fashion is called a roast. Meats and vegetables prepared in this way are described as \"roasted\", e.g., roasted chicken or roasted squash."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Roast_Pig_1.JPG/330px-Roast_Pig_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roasting","wikidata":"Q4865573"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)","wikidata":"Q2932937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/1280px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg/500px-Coffee_beans_unroasted.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Green coffee describes the beans before roasting.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/